         * fired DURING the menu->field->file#14 chain - g_in_park was a RELAY
         * ESCAPEE: the park's exit(0) routes through the R719 atexit door ->
         * R720/R692 shell relay longjmp -> the program re-launches with the
         * latch still set (no clear site existed), and the NEXT ordinary alarm
         * killed the run mid-load. Two-part fix: (1) the latch now resets at
         * every boot-epoch bump (all relay re-entry points); (2) this check
         * remains the c122 protection but only fires on TRUE wedges - a printer
         * genuinely wedged in signal context freezes ALL receipts, so exit only
         * when the receipt counter shows ZERO flow across the alarm window.
         * Receipts flowing = park progressing or game re-launched: re-arm and
