dict order is receipted BEYOND the 50MB cutoff to the fuse; the [hook] watcher print for cell 0x59330 moves to the dedicated [latchhw] tag on that channel. Print policy ONLY - the latch is NOT forced nonzero and the verdict is NOT skipped (that could hide an actual loading failure). The by-tag byte census of run.log.raw runs in the script and NAMES the storm source; the cycle after throttles that print (R1276 precedent) and patches exactly what the receipted loop sequence proves: an incorrect write -> fix the writer; a legitimate reset -> fix the init/ordering that should follow; never armed for this attempt -> fix the missing transition. THE c184 STORY - THE BIGGEST SINGLE-RUN ADVANCE OF THE PROJECT: zrfB fired at the receipted fe1c=1 posture (8 arms, 3 fires, stale-FIFO flush + FDF8 heal + same-poll serve + INT1 deliver each), the system-band walk advanced LBA 0->1->3, and behind it the game advanced FURTHER THAN EVER: STATE 0->1 (the coordinator 80077E88 entered NORMALLY with overlay loaded, pMemStart=800AF5E4 pHeapStart=800C426C), member 14 installed (dest=801DD680), the working game table installed (R1232), file#18 RE-ISSUED NATIVELY (ftab READ ISSUED LBA cell=0x1AA66 FDF8=14360), the fn_80019ACC retry spike fell 43->16 with NEW callers (idx=1 r31=80019C14/8001993C - real dispatches, not the retry loop), and the SCREEN PAINTED 100 PERCENT - all four display regions nonzero, first time in project history (c183: 3 percent, A/B only). THE PAD RECEIPT FLIPPED: ReadControllerButtons entry #245760, btn=BFFF START-HELD (BFFF4000) - the game polls input a quarter-million times and SEES our injected press. THE NEW FIRST-BREAK, receipted by pumpcam x3 + mvloop x3 + ftab: file#14 read sits ARMED BUT IDLE - seek=108997, FDF8=125304 armed (the game stamped BOTH the LBA cell and the size cell), cmd 01 GetStat, act=0, pend=0, data=0/0, A22C=4 - the game polls status bit 0x40 which can NEVER set while the drive is idle (the c179/R1246 class). zrfF is the right composite but the wrong band (seek<150 FE04=0 FDF8==2048). zrfG swaps ONLY the band terms for the receipted posture: seek>=100000, FE04==cd_seek_lba (the game own LBA stamp = current-request provenance, R350), FDF8>0 <300000; the composite stays EXACTLY zrfF: same-poll cd_data_load + cd_read_active=1 so 0x40 computes true on THIS poll, no INT forge, no dispatch, 65536-poll stuck confirm, budget 12. PASS = the drain consumes FDF8 below 125304 + forward execution. REVERT if fire with zero consumption. BASE R1284 = the zrfB FE1C=1 widen (PASSED). BASE R1283 = decline cameras. THE c183 STORY - THE GAME IS ALIVE AND RENDERING: the decline cameras came back EMPTY because the c182 file#2-tail wedge never recurred - trajectory nondeterminism swung to the BEST RUN EVER: the game entered a LIVE menu/render loop - 2.7 BILLION vram writes, 8.6M rects, 120K fills, double-buffer display flipping at (0,0)/(0,240), vram_nz=144939/524288 = 27 percent of VRAM filled, the pad polled (padcell cycling FFF74100/FFFF4000 with our injected START presses), 215 mvloop prints across MANY loop sites (80036760/80036BE0/800317E0/80044E9C - the menu family cycling, not a single spin), four epochs, wall dead. THE STICK, receipted twice: the CD wait posture seek=0 cmd 09 FDF8=0 pend=0 A22C=3 sched=1 FE1C=1 held frozen across every poll print w50-fuse, and the [chg] writer trail names FE1C 0006->0001 at fn 0x80040FCC. zrfB (R1280, the door that served this exact seek=0 family in c175) is in-tree but silent: its FE1C ladder (0/6/7/10/11) never covered state 1. THE FIX: add fe1cA==1u to the ladder - ONE term, receipted, nothing else changes; the two-poll arm confirmation, the 40-fire budget, the stale-FIFO flush, the FDF8 heal, the same-poll cd_data_load, the stale-sched clear, and the INT1 force-deliver all stay exactly as the c175-proven set. PASS = zrfB fires at fe1c=1, FDF8 2048->0, the menu advances - new request at a different LBA, new state-table activity, new screen content, or the fn_80019ACC retry spike (43